// OpenCrab v2 C++17 mirror: cross-language parity test.
//
// Loads the JSON vectors written by the Python reference package through
// cpp/tests/gen_vectors.py (tests/vectors/{prg,dcf,drelu,trunc,r2f,controller,codec,contract,
// costmodel}_vectors.json) and checks that the C++ layers reproduce every value:
//   * PRG: the 64-byte MMO expansion of each seed and the derived sL/sR/vL/vR/tL/tR;
//   * DCF: keys generated by Python (binding layout, wire version 2; P in {1, 2, 3}; payload groups
//     Z_2^64 and Z_t with component-specific Convert words) are parsed
//     by C++ and evaluated on the Python evaluation points; both parties' output shares must be
//     identical to Python's, and the reconstruction must equal beta 1{x < alpha};
//   * DReLU: Python material (P = 1 and P = 2) parsed by C++, both parties' bit and product shares;
//     the KEY_COMPONENT_INDEPENDENCE blind attack run on a batch of Python P = 2 keys must fail
//     on every key (a positive control shows the attack code breaks shared-word correction words);
//   * wire codec: every tag, none (0x08) and bool (0x09) included: C++ encodes the described value
//     to the Python bytes, decodes the Python bytes to the described value, same framed bytes;
//   * numeric contracts: field set, canonical JSON bytes and contract hash;
//   * cost model: on identical coefficients, shapes and environments the predicted mean and sigma
//     (relative 1e-9), the byte, round, message, MAC and material formulas, the fused tournament
//     gate counts and the shared constants of results/calibration/formulas.json;
//   * faithful truncation and ring_to_field: Python material parsed by C++, the open message,
//     each party's output share and the reconstructed plaintext;
//   * controller: the stored survival vector reproduced by the C++ dwell model from the instance's
//     telemetry, and the Python decisions by StateAwareController::decide_with_survival
//     (chosen plan, switched flag, Qhat(keep); q_best / lower bound / u_diff when switched); the
//     scheduled instances (candidates with per-step costs exec_s_by_epoch) are priced step by step,
//     and dropping their lists reproduces the recorded one-shape decision (single_shape);
//   * telemetry: the pooled probe estimator (median RTT, burst over the median burst time minus the
//     smallest ping time, floored) and the frame's cap and floor on Python samples (relative 1e-12).
//
// Usage: test_vectors [vectors_dir]   (default: cpp/tests/vectors, tests/vectors or ./vectors)
//        test_vectors --emit DIR [--kci-keys N]
//            writes cpp_drelu_vectors.json, cpp_codec_vectors.json, cpp_contract_vectors.json and
//            cpp_costmodel_vectors.json (same formats, produced by the C++ implementation) into DIR;
//            python/tests/test_cross_language.py checks them with the Python package.
// A missing vector file is reported as "SKIP <file>: file missing, run python cpp/tests/gen_vectors.py"
// and the remaining files are still checked. Prints "PASS <n> checks" and exits 0, or prints the
// first failing check and exits 1. When every vector file is missing (a wrong directory) nothing
// was compared: the test prints "FAIL: no vector file found in <dir>" and exits 1.
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <cstdint>
#include <cstdio>
#include <cstdlib>
#include <cstring>
#include <fstream>
#include <string>
#include <utility>
#include <variant>
#include <vector>

